/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The International Women's Day campaign for the Gender Equality Alliance \(GEA\) addressed workplace inequality by highlighting the superficiality of traditional celebrations. Through a short film set in a typical workplace, the narrative used engaging dialogues and a clever punchline to challenge customary gifts, such as flowers and symbolic pots, which often mask ongoing injustices. The campaign extended beyond the video by sending branded pots and letters to major employers nationwide, encouraging meaningful discussions on gender-based issues. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
